# Ferra Studio - Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 with App Router
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with custom theme
- **Animation**: Motion (Framer Motion)
- **Font Strategy**: Next.js font optimization (Inter, local fonts)

## Code Style & Formatting
- **Indentation**: Tabs (4-space width)
- **Semicolons**: None
- **Quotes**: Double quotes for strings
- **Plugin**: prettier-plugin-tailwindcss for class sorting

## File Structure & Naming Conventions
- **Components**: kebab-case filenames (e.g., `sticky-header.tsx`, `button-flip.tsx`)
- **Pages**: Next.js App Router convention (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: Single-purpose files in `/lib` (e.g., `utils.ts`, `fonts.ts`)
- **Types**: TypeScript interfaces defined inline or in `/types`

## Component Architecture
- **Client Components**: Mark with `"use client"` directive at top
- **Default Exports**: Use for page and component files
- **Named Exports**: Use for utilities and constants
- **Props Interfaces**: Define inline above component, use PascalCase naming

## Import Organization
1. React/Next.js core imports
2. Third-party libraries
3. Local utilities (`@/lib/*`)
4. Local components (`@/components/*`)
5. Assets and styles

## Path Aliases
- Use `@/*` for all absolute imports from project root
- Example: `@/lib/utils`, `@/components/hero`

## Component Patterns
- **Animation**: Use Motion (motion/react) for animations with `useScroll`, `useTransform`, `motion` components
- **Styling**:
  - Use `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
  - Tailwind classes directly in className
  - Custom colors defined in globals.css `@theme` section
- **Refs**: Use `useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)` for DOM references
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first approach, use `md:` prefix for desktop breakpoints

## Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `Hero`, `StickyHeader`, `ButtonFlip`)
- **Props Interfaces**: ComponentNameProps (e.g., `HeroProps`, `ButtonProps`)
- **Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for data arrays (e.g., `SERVICES_DATA`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (e.g., `handleHover`, `gtagInit`)
- **CSS Custom Properties**: kebab-case with double dash prefix (e.g., `--color-red-primary`)

## Animation Standards
- Use scroll-based animations with `useScroll` hook
- Define animation variants for reusable animations
- Use cubic-bezier easing: `[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]` for smooth entrances
- Implement `whileInView` for viewport-triggered animations
- Use `will-change-transform` for performance optimization

## Color System
- Primary colors use oklch color space
- Custom color names: `bone-white`, `ash-gray`, `red-primary`, `red-secondary`
- Apply via Tailwind: `text-bone-white`, `bg-ash-gray`

## TypeScript Guidelines
- Enable strict mode
- Define explicit return types for exported functions
- Use type imports: `import type { Metadata } from "next"`
- Avoid `any` types

## SEO & Metadata
- Define comprehensive metadata in layout files
- Include OpenGraph and Twitter card metadata
- Use structured data (JSON-LD) for organization schema
- Implement sitemap.ts and robots.ts in app directory

## Performance Considerations
- Use Next.js Image component for all images
- Implement lazy loading for below-fold content
- Use `will-change-transform` for animated elements
- Optimize fonts with next/font loader

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include ARIA labels where necessary
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Maintain focus states with `focus-visible:` variants

## Code Quality
- ESLint configured via eslint.config.mjs
- Suppress linting only when necessary with `/* eslint-disable */`
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Extract reusable logic to `/lib` utilities

## Git Commit Style
Based on recent commits:
- Use concise, imperative mood messages
- Reference issue numbers with # notation
- Examples: "Added projects page", "Fixed sticky-services alignment"

## Development Commands
- `npm run dev` - Start development server
- `npm run build` - Production build
- `npm start` - Start production server
- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint
